# Sloth Drawer — environment variables.
#
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. With none of them set the tool runs fully
# offline against a local Ollama and a local SQLite FTS5 index.
#
# Copy to `.env` for your own notes, or export the variables in your shell.
# `.env` is gitignored; this file is the documentation of what exists.

# --- Tiger Cloud (the optional cloud retrieval backend) ---------------------
# When set, the "tiger" backend (pgvector + pg_textsearch BM25 + RRF) is used
# instead of the local SQLite FTS5 index. ONLY manual chunk text and embeddings
# are sent to this service — never device names, serial numbers, purchase
# dates or service history (RULES.md 3.1a).
# Point it at a DEV service or schema: the app needs DDL.
# SLOTH_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname

# Force a retrieval backend regardless of the DSN: "local" | "tiger".
# SLOTH_RETRIEVAL=local

# --- Ollama (local inference) ----------------------------------------------
# Must resolve to a loopback address; a non-loopback host is a hard error.
# SLOTH_OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434

# --- Embeddings (used only by the tiger backend) ---------------------------
# SLOTH_EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text
# SLOTH_EMBED_DIMS=768

# --- Sentry (optional observability) --------------------------------------
# Without this, tracing is a no-op and the package is not even imported.
# SLOTH_SENTRY_DSN=https://examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0

# --- Project layout (rarely needed) ----------------------------------------
# SLOTH_HOME=/path/to/sloth-drawer
